    "stay_on_level_after_submit": "false",
    "teacher_markdown": "**What to look for:**\r\n\r\n* The response states the app's purpose, meaning the goal or problem it helps with, not just what it looks like.\r\n* The response names a specific action the student took and what the app did in response, and connects it to the purpose (1.1.A.7).\r\n* The response names a believable user and explains why that person would want the app.\r\n\r\n**Common issues:**\r\n\r\n* Describing the screen (\"it has a bird picture\") instead of the purpose.\r\n* Naming an input and output but never connecting them to the purpose.\r\n* Naming a user so broad it says nothing (\"everyone\").\r\n\r\n**Sample response:**\r\nThe purpose of the Bird Quiz app is to teach people facts about birds. I could tell because when I clicked a wrong answer, the app sent me to a losing screen, so it was testing what I know about birds. A person who might use this app is a student who likes animals and wants to learn more about them."
